ommon/resource-uids","classIdentifier":"/conf/api-common","target":"/req/api-common/resource-uids","supporting":false,"state":"exact","candidateMappings":["org.opengis.cite.ogcapiconnectedsystems10.conformance.part1.apicommon.Part1ApiCommonTests#resourceUidsAreValidAndGloballyUnique()"],"reviewedMapping":{"part":1,"test":"/conf/api-common/resource-uids","kind":"exact","implementation":"org.opengis.cite.ogcapiconnectedsystems10.conformance.part1.apicommon.Part1ApiCommonTests#resourceUidsAreValidAndGloballyUnique()","reviewedBy":"Codex Sprint 46 ATS line review","reviewedOn":"2026-07-26","evidence":"The deployed TestNG method consumes all supported canonical resources, gives normative SensorML uniqueId precedence followed by GeoJSON properties.uid and direct extension uid, validates absolute URI syntax, and rejects duplicate UIDs across resource types; focused conflicting-shape and cross-type duplication coverage passes."}},{"part":1,"identifier":"/conf/api-common/resource-uids-types","classIdentifier":"/conf/api-common","target":"/rec/api-common/resource-uids-types","supporting":false,"state":"exact","candidateMappings":["org.opengis.cite.ogcapiconnectedsystems10.conformance.part1.apicommon.Part1ApiCommonTests#resourceUidTypesFollowRecommendation()"],"reviewedMapping":{"part":1,"test":"/conf/api-common/resource-uids-types","kind":"exact","implementation":"org.opengis.cite.ogcapiconnectedsystems10.conformance.part1.apicommon.Part1ApiCommonTests#resourceUidTypesFollowRecommendation()","reviewedBy":"Codex Sprint 46 ATS line review","reviewedOn":"2026-07-26","evidence":"The deployed TestNG method evaluates every retrieved UID, recognizes valid UUID URNs and namespaces in the bundled provenance-recorded IANA Formal and Informal URN Namespaces registry snapshot, and emits TestNG warnings rather than failures for other valid forms; focused recommendation-form and registry-integrity coverage passes."}},{"part":1,"identifier":"/conf/api-common/datetime","classIdentifier":"/conf/api-common","target":"/req/api-common/datetime","supporting":false,"state":"exact","candidateMappings":["org.opengis.cite.ogcapiconnectedsystems10.conformance.part1.apicommon.Part1ApiCommonTests#datetimeUsesValidTime()"],"reviewedMapping":{"part":1,"test":"/conf/api-common/datetime","kind":"exact","implementation":"org.opengis.cite.ogcapiconnectedsystems10.conformance.part1.apicommon.Part1ApiCommonTests#datetimeUsesValidTime()","reviewedBy":"Codex Sprint 46 ATS line review","reviewedOn":"2026-07-26","evidence":"The deployed TestNG method iterates advertised collections with temporal extents, queries released collection-items with instant, bounded, open-start, and open-end datetime forms, resolves now at captured request time, rejects non-intersecting validTime, requires unfiltered timeless IDs in every filtered result, and SKIPs with no eligible collection; focused positive, boundary, and fail-closed temporal coverage passes."}},{"part":1,"identifier":"/conf/system/location","classIdentifier":"/conf/system","target":"/rec/system/location","supporting":false,"state":"exact","candidateMappings":["org.opengis.cite.ogcapiconnectedsystems10.conformance.systemfeatures.SystemFeaturesTests#systemLocationsFollowRecommendation()"],"reviewedMapping":{"part":1,"test":"/conf/system/location","kind":"exact","implementation":"org.opengis.cite.ogcapiconnectedsystems10.conformance.systemfeatures.SystemFeaturesTests#systemLocationsFollowRecommendation()","reviewedBy":"Codex Sprint 47 ATS line review","reviewedOn":"2026-07-26","evidence":"The deployed TestNG method evaluates every canonical System page, applies the released GeoJSON geometry and SensorML position mappings, exempts only Simulation and Process assets, and reports recommendation warnings without converting them to conformance failures."}},{"part":1,"identifier":"/conf/system/location-time","classIdentifier":"/conf/system","target":"/req/system/location-time","supporting":false,"state":"exact","candidateMappings":["org.opengis.cite.ogcapiconnectedsystems10.conformance.systemfeatures.SystemFeaturesTests#mobileSystemLocationIsUpdated()"],"reviewedMapping":{"part":1,"test":"/conf/system/location-time","kind":"exact","implementation":"org.opengis.cite.ogcapiconnectedsystems10.conformance.systemfeatures.SystemFeaturesTests#mobileSystemLocationIsUpdated()","reviewedBy":"Codex Sprint 47 ATS line review","reviewedOn":"2026-07-26","evidence":"The deployed TestNG method accepts the optional public mobile-system-id argument, dereferences that known moving System, applies representation-specific coordinate mappings, and requires a position change during bounded 30-second polling; SensorML orientation-only changes do not prove movement, and absent input produces an explicit SKIP rather than positive evidence."}},{"part":1,"identifier":"/conf/system/canonical-url","classIdentifier":"/conf/system","target":"/req/system/canonical-url","supporting":false,"state":"exact","candidateMappings":["org.opengis.cite.ogcapiconnectedsystems10.conformance.systemfeatures.SystemFeaturesTests#everySystemHasCanonicalUrl()"],"reviewedMapping":{"part":1,"test":"/conf/system/canonical-url","kind":"exact","implementation":"org.opengis.cite.ogcapiconnectedsystems10.conformance.systemfeatures.SystemFeaturesTests#everySystemHasCanonicalUrl()","reviewedBy":"Codex Sprint 47 ATS line review","reviewedOn":"2026-07-26","evidence":"The deployed TestNG method traverses every advertised sosa:System collection through the reviewed collection-items helper, requires one same-origin canonical URL per item, dereferences it with the source representation media type, and compares complete parsed content after removing only canonical links."}},{"part":1,"identifier":"/conf/system/resources-endpoint","classIdentifier":"/conf/system","target":"/req/system/resources-endpoint","supporting":false,"state":"exact","candidateMappings":["org.opengis.cite.ogcapiconnectedsystems10.conformance.systemfeatures.SystemFeaturesTests#systemResourcesEndpointIsValid()"],"reviewedMapping":{"part":1,"test":"/conf/system/resources-endpoint","kind":"exact","implementation":"org.opengis.cite.ogcapiconnectedsystems10.conformance.systemfeatures.SystemFeaturesTests#systemResourcesEndpointIsValid()","reviewedBy":"Codex Sprint 47 ATS line review","reviewedOn":"2026-07-26","evidence":"The deployed TestNG method retrieves its own canonical System evidence and invokes the endpoint-parameterized resources procedure for /systems. Every page is validated against the bundled released GeoJSON or SensorML System collection schema selected from the actual response media type; the complete pinned GeoJSON dependencies are provenance-bound by SHA-256, malformed wrappers/features/geometries fail closed, and unsupported media produces an explicit SKIP."}},{"part":1,"identifier":"/conf/system/canonical-endpoint","classIdentifier":"/conf/system","target":"/req/system/canonical-endpoint","supporting":false,"state":"exact","candidateMappings":["org.opengis.cite.ogcapiconnectedsystems10.conformance.systemfeatures.SystemFeaturesTests#canonicalSystemsEndpointIsValid()"],"reviewedMapping":{"part":1,"test":"/conf/system/canonical-endpoint","kind":"exact","implementation":"org.opengis.cite.ogcapiconnectedsystems10.conformance.systemfeatures.SystemFeaturesTests#canonicalSystemsEndpointIsValid()","reviewedBy":"Codex Sprint 47 ATS line review","reviewedOn":"2026-07-26","evidence":"The independently executable deployed TestNG method retrieves its own evidence and executes the endpoint-parameterized released resources procedure against the fixed API-root /systems canonical endpoint through the reviewed canonical-resources traversal, including HTTP, media-type, pagination, collection-shape, and fail-closed schema evidence."}},{"part":1,"identifier":"/conf/system/collections","classIdentifier":"/conf/system","target":"/req/system/collections","supporting":false,"state":"exact","candidateMappings":["org.opengis.cite.ogcapiconnectedsystems10.conformance.systemfeatures.SystemFeaturesTests#systemCollectionsAreValid()"],"reviewedMapping":{"part":1,"test":"/conf/system/collections","kind":"exact","implementation":"org.opengis.cite.ogcapiconnectedsystems10.conformance.systemfeatures.SystemFeaturesTests#systemCollectionsAreValid()","reviewedBy":"Codex Sprint 47 ATS line review","reviewedOn":"2026-07-26","evidence":"The independently executable deployed TestNG method selects every /collections entry with featureType=sosa:System, continues after unsupported collections, traverses every supported items page through the reviewed helper, invokes the same endpoint-parameterized schema procedure, and restricts each representation-specific System type to the five released SOSA URI or CURIE values. Direct HTTP regression coverage proves an earlier unsupported collection cannot hide a later invalid supported collection. It deliberately adds no collection-existence or itemType assertion absent from the released Annex A procedure."}},{"part":1,"identifier":"/conf/subsystem/collection","classIdentifier":"/conf/subsystem","target":"/req/subsystem/collection","supporting":false,"state":"exact","candidateMappings":["org.opengis.cite.ogcapiconnectedsystems10.conformance.subsystems.SubsystemsTests#subsystemCollectionIsValid()"],"reviewedMapping":{"part":1,"test":"/conf/subsystem/collection","kind":"exact","implementation":"org.opengis.cite.ogcapiconnectedsystems10.conformance.subsystems.SubsystemsTests#subsystemCollectionIsValid()","reviewedBy":"Codex Sprint 48 ATS line review","reviewedOn":"2026-07-26","evidence":"The independently executable deployed TestNG method probes bounded, media-gated nested collections to select a parent with a nonempty subsystem collection without requiring local item ids, dereferences that parent System resource, counts exactly one rel=subsystems link occurrence, and requires its resolved URI to exactly equal the already-fetched api_root/systems/{id}/subsystems endpoint. It rejects duplicate-identical, trailing-slash, query, fragment, and cross-origin variants, reuses the accepted first response, establishes HTTP 200 and actual media before parsing every page, warns and SKIPs unsupported or absent media, and validates every supported page against the existing released GeoJSON or SensorML System collection schema."}},{"part":1,"identifier":"/conf/subsystem/recursive-param","classIdentifier":"/conf/subsystem","target":"/req/subsystem/recursive-param","supporting":false,"state":"exact","candidateMappings":["org.opengis.cite.ogcapiconnectedsystems10.conformance.subsystems.SubsystemsTests#recursiveParameterUsesBooleanValues()"],"reviewedMapping":{"part":1,"test":"/conf/subsystem/recursive-param","kind":"exact","implementation":"org.opengis.cite.ogcapiconnectedsystems10.conformance.subsystems.SubsystemsTests#recursiveParameterUsesBooleanValues()","reviewedBy":"Codex Sprint 48 ATS line review","reviewedOn":"2026-07-26","evidence":"The independently executable deployed TestNG method issues read-only /systems requests with the exact recursive=false and recursive=true query values and requires HTTP 200 for both without parsing representation content outside the released procedure. Controlled HTTP coverage records both exact query strings and proves successful non-JSON responses do not create unrelated failures."}},{"part":1,"identifier":"/conf/subsystem/recursive-search-systems","classIdentifier":"/conf/subsystem","target":"/req/subsystem/recursive-search-systems","supporting":false,"state":"exact","candidateMappings":["org.opengis.cite.ogcapiconnectedsystems10.conformance.subsystems.SubsystemsTests#systemsRecursiveSearchIsComplete()"],"reviewedMapping":{"part":1,"test":"/conf/subsystem/recursive-search-systems","kind":"exact","implementation":"org.opengis.cite.ogcapiconnectedsystems10.conformance.subsystems.SubsystemsTests#systemsRecursiveSearchIsComplete()","reviewedBy":"Codex Sprint 48 ATS line review","reviewedOn":"2026-07-26","evidence":"The deployed TestNG method builds a bounded, iteratively cycle-rejecting hierarchy oracle solely from default direct-child subsystem endpoints, rejects shortcut overlap when a direct child is also reachable through a longer path, then proves default and recursive=false /systems exclude every discovered child while recursive=true includes all independently discovered hierarchy nodes. Blank and duplicate resource ids fail closed; absent hierarchy data produces an explicit SKIP."}},{"part":1,"identifier":"/conf/subsystem/recursive-search-subsystems","classIdentifier":"/conf/subsystem","target":"/req/subsystem/recursive-search-subsystems","supporting":false,"state":"exact","candidateMappings":["org.opengis.cite.ogcapiconnectedsystems10.conformance.subsystems.SubsystemsTests#subsystemsRecursiveSearchIsComplete()"],"reviewedMapping":{"part":1,"test":"/conf/subsystem/recursive-search-subsystems","kind":"exact","implementation":"org.opengis.cite.ogcapiconnectedsystems10.conformance.subsystems.SubsystemsTests#subsystemsRecursiveSearchIsComplete()","reviewedBy":"Codex Sprint 48 ATS line review","reviewedOn":"2026-07-26","evidence":"The deployed TestNG method selects a parent with independently established transitive descendants, rejects direct-child shortcut overlap before evidence selection, proves default and recursive=false nested endpoints contain exactly direct children, and proves recursive=true contains every descendant. It never derives expected hierarchy membership from the recursive=true response itself."}},{"part":1,"identifier":"/conf/subsystem/recursive-assoc","classIdentifier":"/conf/subsystem","target":"/req/subsystem/recursive-assoc","supporting":false,"state":"exact","candidateMappings":["org.opengis.cite.ogcapiconnectedsystems10.conformance.subsystems.SubsystemsTests#nestedAssociationsAreIncluded()"],"reviewedMapping":{"part":1,"test":"/conf/subsystem/recursive-assoc","kind":"exact","implementation":"org.opengis.cite.ogcapiconnectedsystems10.conformance.subsystems.SubsystemsTests#nestedAssociationsAreIncluded()","reviewedBy":"Codex Sprint 48 ATS line review","reviewedOn":"2026-07-26","evidence":"For every independently discovered parent with subsystems, the deployed TestNG method probes canonical top-level samplingFeatures, datastreams, and controlstreams endpoints as independent implementation evidence. Once a type returns HTTP 200 there, every parent and descendant nested endpoint must return HTTP 200; all-parent 404 cannot become an unsupported-type SKIP. The method unions descendant resource ids and requires each parent endpoint to contain that closure. Top-level-unsupported types and an entirely empty descendant evidence set produce explicit SKIPs rather than positive conformance."}},{"part":1,"identifier":"/conf/deployment/canonical-url","classIdentifier":"/conf/deployment","target":"/req/deployment/canonical-url","supporting":false,"state":"exact","candidateMappings":["org.opengis.cite.ogcapiconnectedsystems10.conformance.deployments.DeploymentsTests#everyDeploymentHasCanonicalUrl()"],"reviewedMapping":{"part":1,"test":"/conf/deployment/canonical-url","kind":"exact","implementation":"org.opengis.cite.ogcapiconnectedsystems10.conformance.deployments.DeploymentsTests#everyDeploymentHasCanonicalUrl()","reviewedBy":"Codex Sprint 49 ATS line review","reviewedOn":"2026-07-26","evidence":"The independently executable deployed TestNG method selects every advertised collection with exact featureType=sosa:Deployment, traverses each through the reviewed API Common collection-items procedure, and evaluates every returned item. It requires at least one canonical link and validates every canonical occurrence as the same-origin api_root/deployments/{encoded id} identity while allowing duplicate or representation-query variants; it dereferences the first occurrence deterministically with its advertised representation or source-page media type, requires HTTP 200, and compares complete parsed content after removing only top-level canonical links. Missing Deployment collections fail and unsupported selected collections SKIP instead of yielding partial positive evidence."}},{"part":1,"identifier":"/conf/deployment/resources-endpoint","classIdentifier":"/conf/deployment","target":"/req/deployment/resources-endpoint","supporting":false,"state":"exact","candidateMappings":["org.opengis.cite.ogcapiconnectedsystems10.conformance.deployments.DeploymentsTests#deploymentResourcesEndpointIsValid()"],"reviewedMapping":{"part":1,"test":"/conf/deployment/resources-endpoint","kind":"exact","implementation":"org.opengis.cite.ogcapiconnectedsystems10.conformance.deployments.DeploymentsTests#deploymentResourcesEndpointIsValid()","reviewedBy":"Codex Sprint 49 ATS line review","reviewedOn":"2026-07-26","evidence":"The independently executable deployed TestNG method invokes the endpoint-parameterized released resources procedure against /deployments, requires HTTP 200, gates every page by its actual GeoJSON or SensorML media type before parsing, traverses bounded same-origin pagination, and validates every page against the corresponding bundled released Deployment collection schema. HTTP 404 fails; unsupported actual media produces an explicit SKIP."}},{"part":1,"identifier":"/conf/deployment/canonical-endpoint","classIdentifier":"/conf/deployment","target":"/req/deployment/canonical-endpoint","supporting":false,"state":"exact","candidateMappings":["org.opengis.cite.ogcapiconnectedsystems10.conformance.deployments.DeploymentsTests#canonicalDeploymentsEndpointIsValid()"],"reviewedMapping":{"part":1,"test":"/conf/deployment/canonical-endpoint","kind":"exact","implementation":"org.opengis.cite.ogcapiconnectedsystems10.conformance.deployments.DeploymentsTests#canonicalDeploymentsEndpointIsValid()","reviewedBy":"Codex Sprint 49 ATS line review","reviewedOn":"2026-07-26","evidence":"The independently executable deployed TestNG method supplies the fixed api_root/deployments URL to the same released endpoint-parameterized resources procedure. It independently retrieves, media-gates, paginates, and schema-validates the canonical endpoint rather than depending on another Deployment test method."}},{"part":1,"identifier":"/conf/deployment/collections","classIdentifier":"/conf/deployment","target":"/req/deployment/collections","supporting":false,"state":"exact","candidateMappings":["org.opengis.cite.ogcapiconnectedsystems10.conformance.deployments.DeploymentsTests#deploymentCollectionsAreValid()"],"reviewedMapping":{"part":1,"test":"/conf/deployment/collections","kind":"exact","implementation":"org.opengis.cite.ogcapiconnectedsystems10.conformance.deployments.DeploymentsTests#deploymentCollectionsAreValid()","reviewedBy":"Codex Sprint 49 ATS line review","reviewedOn":"2026-07-26","evidence":"The independently executable deployed TestNG method retrieves /collections, selects every exact featureType=sosa:Deployment entry, requires itemType=feature and a nonempty id, and traverses every selected items endpoint through the reviewed API Common helper with an additional actual-media gate on every page. Every supported GeoJSON or SensorML page is validated against the corresponding bundled released Deployment collection schema; no advertised Deployment collection fails and unsupported evidence SKIPs."}},{"part":1,"identifier":"/conf/deployment/ref-from-system","classIdentifier":"/conf/deployment","target":"/req/deployment/ref-from-system","supporting":false,"state":"exact","candidateMappings":["org.opengis.cite.ogcapiconnectedsystems10.conformance.deployments.DeploymentsTests#deploymentsReferencedFromSystemsAreValid()"],"reviewedMapping":{"part":1,"test":"/conf/deployment/ref-from-system","kind":"exact","implementation":"org.opengis.cite.ogcapiconnectedsystems10.conformance.deployments.DeploymentsTests#deploymentsReferencedFromSystemsAreValid()","reviewedBy":"Codex Sprint 49 ATS line review","reviewedOn":"2026-07-26","evidence":"The independently executable deployed TestNG method retrieves all canonical Systems through the reviewed API Common procedure, then requests and completely paginates systems/{encoded id}/deployments for every System. It gates each page by actual GeoJSON or SensorML media before parsing, validates the released Deployment collection schema, and requires every Deployment to contain the representation-specific owning-System reference: GeoJSON properties.deployedSystems@link or SensorML deployedSystems[].system.href. Matching is exact on same-origin canonical System path, preventing prefix, substring, cross-origin, and fragment false positives."}},{"part":1,"identifier":"/conf/subdeployment/collection","classIdentifier":"/conf/subdeployment","target":"/req/subdeployment/collection","supporting":false,"state":"exact","candidateMappings":["org.opengis.cite.ogcapiconnectedsystems10.conformance.subdeployments.SubdeploymentsTests#subdeploymentCollectionIsValid()"],"reviewedMapping":{"part":1,"test":"/conf/subdeployment/collection","kind":"exact","implementation":"org.opengis.cite.ogcapiconnectedsystems10.conformance.subdeployments.SubdeploymentsTests#subdeploymentCollectionIsValid()","reviewedBy":"Codex Sprint 51 ATS line review and post-Raze correction","reviewedOn":"2026-07-27","evidence":"The independently executable deployed TestNG method discovers every parent with direct Subdeployments through bounded, actual-media-gated hierarchy traversal. For each parent it retrieves the canonical Deployment, requires every rel=subdeployments occurrence to resolve to the normalized same-origin api_root/deployments/{encoded id}/subdeployments target without query or fragment, and accepts equivalent explicit default ports and percent-encoded unreserved path characters. It then requires HTTP 200, bounded same-origin pagination, and released GeoJSON or SensorML Deployment collection schema validity on every page. No hierarchy data produces an explicit SKIP."}},{"part":1,"identifier":"/conf/subdeployment/recursive-param","classIdentifier":"/conf/subdeployment","target":"/req/subdeployment/recursive-param","supporting":false,"state":"exact","candidateMappings":["org.opengis.cite.ogcapiconnectedsystems10.conformance.subdeployments.SubdeploymentsTests#recursiveParameterUsesBooleanValues()"],"reviewedMapping":{"part":1,"test":"/conf/subdeployment/recursive-param","kind":"exact","implementation":"org.opengis.cite.ogcapiconnectedsystems10.conformance.subdeployments.SubdeploymentsTests#recursiveParameterUsesBooleanValues()","reviewedBy":"Codex Sprint 51 ATS line review and post-Raze correction","reviewedOn":"2026-07-27","evidence":"The independently executable deployed TestNG method issues read-only /deployments requests with the exact recursive=false and recursive=true query values and requires HTTP 200 for both. It deliberately makes a status-only comparison and does not parse or impose representation-media constraints absent from the released procedure; controlled HTTP coverage proves both exact requests execute against successful non-JSON responses."}},{"part":1,"identifier":"/conf/subdeployment/recursive-search-deployments","classIdentifier":"/conf/subdeployment","target":"/req/subdeployment/recursive-search-deployments","supporting":false,"state":"exact","candidateMappings":["org.opengis.cite.ogcapiconnectedsystems10.conformance.subdeployments.SubdeploymentsTests#deploymentsRecursiveSearchIsComplete()"],"reviewedMapping":{"part":1,"test":"/conf/subdeployment/recursive-search-deployments","kind":"exact","implementation":"org.opengis.cite.ogcapiconnectedsystems10.conformance.subdeployments.SubdeploymentsTests#deploymentsRecursiveSearchIsComplete()","reviewedBy":"Codex Sprint 51 ATS line review and post-Raze correction","reviewedOn":"2026-07-27","evidence":"The deployed TestNG method independently builds a bounded Deployment hierarchy solely from default direct-child Subdeployment endpoints, with every page gated by actual GeoJSON or SensorML media and validated against the released Deployment schema. Duplicate ids, multiple parents, cycles, shortcut edges, and safety-bound overflow fail closed. It proves default and recursive=false /deployments results equal exactly the hierarchy roots and recursive=true equals every discovered node; absent hierarchy data explicitly SKIPs."}},{"part":1,"identifier":"/conf/subdeployment/recursive-search-subdeployments","classIdentifier":"/conf/subdeployment","target":"/req/subdeployment/recursive-search-subdeployments","supporting":false,"state":"exact","candidateMappings":["org.opengis.cite.ogcapiconnectedsystems10.conformance.subdeployments.SubdeploymentsTests#subdeploymentsRecursiveSearchIsComplete()"],"reviewedMapping":{"part":1,"test":"/conf/subdeployment/recursive-search-subdeployments","kind":"exact","implementation":"org.opengis.cite.ogcapiconnectedsystems10.conformance.subdeployments.SubdeploymentsTests#subdeploymentsRecursiveSearchIsComplete()","reviewedBy":"Codex Sprint 51 ATS line review and post-Raze correction","reviewedOn":"2026-07-27","evidence":"The deployed TestNG method independently discovers a parent with direct and transitive Subdeployments through bounded, schema-validated, actual-media-gated default hierarchy traversal. It proves that parent's default and recursive=false nested endpoint results equal exactly its direct children while recursive=true equals every descendant. Expected membership is never derived from a recursive=true response, and no transitive hierarchy produces an explicit SKIP."}},{"part":1,"identifier":"/conf/subdeployment/recursive-assoc","classIdentifier":"/conf/subdeployment","target":"/req/subdeployment/recursive-assoc","supporting":false,"state":"exact","candidateMappings":["org.opengis.cite.ogcapiconnectedsystems10.conformance.subdeployments.SubdeploymentsTests#recursiveAssociationsIncludeDescendants()"],"reviewedMapping":{"part":1,"test":"/conf/subdeployment/recursive-assoc","kind":"exact","implementation":"org.opengis.cite.ogcapiconnectedsystems10.conformance.subdeployments.SubdeploymentsTests#recursiveAssociationsIncludeDescendants()","reviewedBy":"Codex Sprint 51 ATS line review and post-Raze correction","reviewedOn":"2026-07-27","evidence":"For each independently discovered parent with direct Subdeployments, the deployed TestNG method inspects deployedSystems, featuresOfInterest, samplingFeatures, datastreams, and controlstreams. For every advertised relation it selects a safe same-origin JSON-compatible link across all occurrences, preferring typed JSON while allowing actual-media-gated untyped negotiation and refusing cross-origin or unsupported candidates. The optional public fixture independently identifies directly owned ids for the parent and every descendant; their complete union is required in the parent endpoint. Missing fixture coverage, no safe comparable link, or no advertised relation explicitly SKIPs, while any observed parent-owned or descendant-owned omission fails."}},{"part":1,"identifier":"/conf/procedure/location","classIdentifier":"/conf/procedure","target":"/req/procedure/location","supporting":false,"state":"exact","candidateMappings":["org.opengis.cite.ogcapiconnectedsystems10.conformance.procedures.ProceduresTests#procedureLocationIsAbsent()"],"reviewedMapping":{"part":1,"test":"/conf/procedure/location","kind":"exact","implementation":"org.opengis.cite.ogcapiconnectedsystems10.conformance.procedures.ProceduresTests#procedureLocationIsAbsent()","reviewedBy":"Codex Sprint 50 ATS line review","reviewedOn":"2026-07-26","evidence":"The independently executable deployed TestNG method retrieves and completely paginates the canonical /procedures endpoint. It gates every page by actual GeoJSON or SensorML media before evaluating items, requires every GeoJSON Procedure to contain geometry set to null, and requires every SensorML Procedure to omit the position member. Unsupported actual media produces an explicit SKIP and cannot become positive evidence."}},{"part":1,"identifier":"/conf/procedure/canonical-url","classIdentifier":"/conf/procedure","target":"/req/procedure/canonical-url","supporting":false,"state":"exact","candidateMappings":["org.opengis.cite.ogcapiconnectedsystems10.conformance.procedures.ProceduresTests#everyProcedureHasCanonicalUrl()"],"reviewedMapping":{"part":1,"test":"/conf/procedure/canonical-url","kind":"exact","implementation":"org.opengis.cite.ogcapiconnectedsystems10.conformance.procedures.ProceduresTests#everyProcedureHasCanonicalUrl()","reviewedBy":"Codex Sprint 50 ATS line review","reviewedOn":"2026-07-26","evidence":"The independently executable deployed TestNG method selects every advertised collection with exact featureType=sosa:Procedure, traverses each through the reviewed API Common collection-items procedure, and evaluates every returned item. It requires at least one canonical link and validates every canonical occurrence as the same-origin api_root/procedures/{encoded id} identity while allowing duplicate or representation-query variants. It dereferences the first occurrence whose advertised media is absent or matches the collection page, requires HTTP 200 and comparable negotiated media, and compares complete parsed content after removing top-level canonical links; a links member emptied by canonical-link removal is normalized to omitted. No comparable occurrence warns and SKIPs, and missing Procedure collections fail."}},{"part":1,"identifier":"/conf/procedure/resources-endpoint","classIdentifier":"/conf/procedure","target":"/req/procedure/resources-endpoint","supporting":false,"state":"exact","candidateMappings":["org.opengis.cite.ogcapiconnectedsystems10.conformance.procedures.ProceduresTests#procedureResourcesEndpointIsValid()"],"reviewedMapping":{"part":1,"test":"/conf/procedure/resources-endpoint","kind":"exact","implementation":"org.opengis.cite.ogcapiconnectedsystems10.conformance.procedures.ProceduresTests#procedureResourcesEndpointIsValid()","reviewedBy":"Codex Sprint 50 ATS line review","reviewedOn":"2026-07-26","evidence":"The independently executable deployed TestNG method invokes the endpoint-parameterized released resources procedure against /procedures, requires HTTP 200, gates every page by its actual GeoJSON or SensorML media type before parsing, traverses bounded same-origin pagination, and validates every page against the corresponding bundled released Procedure collection schema. It also verifies every item uses one of the nine released Procedure types in CURIE or URI form. HTTP 404 fails; unsupported actual media produces an explicit SKIP."}},{"part":1,"identifier":"/conf/procedure/canonical-endpoint","classIdentifier":"/conf/procedure","target":"/req/procedure/canonical-endpoint","supporting":false,"state":"exact","candidateMappings":["org.opengis.cite.ogcapiconnectedsystems10.conformance.procedures.ProceduresTests#canonicalProceduresEndpointIsValid()"],"reviewedMapping":{"part":1,"test":"/conf/procedure/canonical-endpoint","kind":"exact","implementation":"org.opengis.cite.ogcapiconnectedsystems10.conformance.procedures.ProceduresTests#canonicalProceduresEndpointIsValid()","reviewedBy":"Codex Sprint 50 ATS line review","reviewedOn":"2026-07-26","evidence":"The independently executable deployed TestNG method supplies the fixed api_root/procedures URL to the same released endpoint-parameterized resources procedure. It independently retrieves, media-gates, paginates, schema-validates, and validates Procedure types at the canonical endpoint without depending on another Procedure test method."}},{"part":1,"identifier":"/conf/procedure/collections","classIdentifier":"/conf/procedure","target":"/req/procedure/collections","supporting":false,"state":"exact","candidateMappings":["org.opengis.cite.ogcapiconnectedsystems10.conformance.procedures.ProceduresTests#procedureCollectionsAreValid()"],"reviewedMapping":{"part":1,"test":"/conf/procedure/collections","kind":"exact","implementation":"org.opengis.cite.ogcapiconnectedsystems10.conformance.procedures.ProceduresTests#procedureCollectionsAreValid()","reviewedBy":"Codex Sprint 50 ATS line review","reviewedOn":"2026-07-26","evidence":"The independently executable deployed TestNG method retrieves /collections, selects every exact featureType=sosa:Procedure entry, requires itemType=feature and a nonempty id, and traverses every selected items endpoint through the reviewed API Common helper with an additional actual-media gate on every page. Every supported GeoJSON or SensorML page is validated against the corresponding bundled released Procedure collection schema and every item is checked against the nine released Procedure types in CURIE or URI form; no advertised Procedure collection fails and unsupported evidence SKIPs."}},{"part":1,"identifier":"/conf/sf/canonical-url","classIdentifier":"/conf/sf","target":"/req/sf/canonical-url","supporting":false,"state":"exact","candidateMappings":["org.opengis.cite.ogcapiconnectedsystems10.conformance.samplingfeatures.SamplingFeaturesTests#everySamplingFeatureHasCanonicalUrl()"],"reviewedMapping":{"part":1,"test":"/conf/sf/canonical-url","kind":"exact","implementation":"org.opengis.cite.ogcapiconnectedsystems10.conformance.samplingfeatures.SamplingFeaturesTests#everySamplingFeatureHasCanonicalUrl()","reviewedBy":"Codex Sprint 52 ATS line review","reviewedOn":"2026-07-27","evidence":"The independently executable deployed TestNG method selects every exact featureType=sosa:Sample collection and observes every safely parsed supported GeoJSON items page before pagination advances. For every item it validates all canonical-link occurrences as same-origin api_root/samplingFeatures/{encoded id} identities, dereferences a representation-compatible occurrence, requires HTTP 200 and comparable actual media, and compares complete parsed content after removing only top-level canonical links. Expected media or comparability limitations are accumulated at collection and item boundaries so later inspectable defects still fail before one aggregate evidence SKIP."}},{"part":1,"identifier":"/conf/sf/resources-endpoint","classIdentifier":"/conf/sf","target":"/req/sf/resources-endpoint","supporting":false,"state":"exact","candidateMappings":["org.opengis.cite.ogcapiconnectedsystems10.conformance.samplingfeatures.SamplingFeaturesTests#samplingFeaturesResourcesEndpointIsValid()"],"reviewedMapping":{"part":1,"test":"/conf/sf/resources-endpoint","kind":"exact","implementation":"org.opengis.cite.ogcapiconnectedsystems10.conformance.samplingfeatures.SamplingFeaturesTests#samplingFeaturesResourcesEndpointIsValid()","reviewedBy":"Codex Sprint 52 ATS line review","reviewedOn":"2026-07-27","evidence":"The independently executable deployed TestNG method invokes the endpoint-parameterized released resources procedure against /samplingFeatures, requires HTTP 200, gates every page by actual GeoJSON media before parsing, traverses bounded same-origin pagination, and validates every page against the bundled released Sampling Feature collection schema. HTTP 404 fails and unsupported actual media produces an explicit SKIP."}},{"part":1,"identifier":"/conf/sf/canonical-endpoint","classIdentifier":"/conf/sf","target":"/req/sf/canonical-endpoint","supporting":false,"state":"exact","candidateMappings":["org.opengis.cite.ogcapiconnectedsystems10.conformance.samplingfeatures.SamplingFeaturesTests#canonicalSamplingFeaturesEndpointIsValid()"],"reviewedMapping":{"part":1,"test":"/conf/sf/canonical-endpoint","kind":"exact","implementation":"org.opengis.cite.ogcapiconnectedsystems10.conformance.samplingfeatures.SamplingFeaturesTests#canonicalSamplingFeaturesEndpointIsValid()","reviewedBy":"Codex Sprint 52 ATS line review","reviewedOn":"2026-07-27","evidence":"The independently executable deployed TestNG method supplies the fixed api_root/samplingFeatures URL to the same released endpoint-parameterized resources procedure. It independently retrieves, media-gates, paginates, and schema-validates the canonical endpoint without depending on another Sampling Features method."}},{"part":1,"identifier":"/conf/sf/collections","classIdentifier":"/conf/sf","target":"/req/sf/collections","supporting":false,"state":"exact","candidateMappings":["org.opengis.cite.ogcapiconnectedsystems10.conformance.samplingfeatures.SamplingFeaturesTests#samplingFeatureCollectionsAreValid()"],"reviewedMapping":{"part":1,"test":"/conf/sf/collections","kind":"exact","implementation":"org.opengis.cite.ogcapiconnectedsystems10.conformance.samplingfeatures.SamplingFeaturesTests#samplingFeatureCollectionsAreValid()","reviewedBy":"Codex Sprint 52 ATS line review","reviewedOn":"2026-07-27","evidence":"The independently executable deployed TestNG method retrieves /collections, selects every exact featureType=sosa:Sample entry, requires itemType=feature and a nonempty id, and traverses every selected items endpoint through the reviewed API Common helper with an actual GeoJSON media gate on every page. A page observer schema-validates each safely parsed supported page before pagination advances, so a later media SKIP cannot erase an earlier schema failure. Expected media limitations are accumulated per collection so later inspectable defects still fail before one aggregate evidence SKIP."}},{"part":1,"identifier":"/conf/sf/ref-from-system","classIdentifier":"/conf/sf","target":"/req/sf/ref-from-system","supporting":false,"state":"exact","candidateMappings":["org.opengis.cite.ogcapiconnectedsystems10.conformance.samplingfeatures.SamplingFeaturesTests#samplingFeaturesAreAvailableFromEverySystem()"],"reviewedMapping":{"part":1,"test":"/conf/sf/ref-from-system","kind":"exact","implementation":"org.opengis.cite.ogcapiconnectedsystems10.conformance.samplingfeatures.SamplingFeaturesTests#samplingFeaturesAreAvailableFromEverySystem()","reviewedBy":"Codex Sprint 52 ATS line review","reviewedOn":"2026-07-27","evidence":"The independently executable deployed TestNG method retrieves every canonical System through the reviewed API Common procedure and then requests systems/{encoded id}/samplingFeatures for every System. It requires HTTP 200, co